---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const description =
  'Engineering background, running and race directing outside of work, and links to the resume and LinkedIn.';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={description}>
  <h1 class="text-4xl text-ink">About</h1>
  <div class="mt-8 max-w-[65ch] space-y-4">
    <p>
      Software engineer with five years in production, in Python, TypeScript, and AWS. At Point
      Loma Nazarene University I own enterprise integrations and the CI/CD standards around them:
      daily Workday feeds, the GitHub migration, and test gates on services that used to deploy
      without them.
    </p>
    <p>
      At CampLife I built the ETL pipeline that became the standard onboarding path for a
      multi-tenant platform serving 600+ campground clients. Parks arrived with exports from
      Newbook, RMS, paper ledgers, and spreadsheets. The work was schema detection, validation,
      and deduplication, then staying with the system when a million-row file broke the first
      design. I also worked with the CEO and COO on occupancy analysis presented at the 2024
      CampEx conference.
    </p>
    <p>
      I started writing Python at 12. The work since then runs from personal scripts to systems
      other people run in production.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Outside of work</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 max-w-[65ch] space-y-4">
      <p>
        I spend a lot of free time training for road and trail races, mostly in Chattanooga and
        also elsewhere in the country. I coach runners as a hobby. I earned a UESCA running
        coaching certification in April 2025.
      </p>
      <p>
        From August 2021 to September 2025 I was part-time Director of White Oak Mountain Racing
        at Southern Adventist University in Collegedale. I directed over 10 races for the
        university and community clients. Some events had 500+ participants. One race raised over
        $7k for outdoor education for local inner city school children.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">How I work</h2>
    <ul class="mt-6 max-w-[65ch] list-disc space-y-3 pl-5">
      <li>Own the system from design through production, including the logs, reports, and deploy gates.</li>
      <li>Verify the behavior of the core path. A coverage number is not the point.</li>
      <li>Work directly with the people who use the system, including onboarding leads and executives.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Resume</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-4">
      <a
        href={site.resumePath}
        class="rounded-[2px] bg-accent px-4 py-2 text-sm text-white hover:bg-accent-dark"
      >
        Download resume
      </a>
      <a
        href={site.linkedin}
        class="text-sm text-ink underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent hover:underline"
      >
        LinkedIn
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
